  "contracts": [
    "Every application group has separate native Valkey, replacement Valkey, PostgreSQL, MySQL and S3-compatible object-store fixtures. Tests run serially within a group.",
    "The operator group builds cmd/starport in its selected pure or race mode from unchanged source. Binary bytes, command owner, Go1.27.1, source revision, native architecture, CGO and race settings are retained and checked.",
    "Named Go JSON events must include each selected owner exactly once, every critical subcase, and a single successful package completion. Any skip, failure, foreign package, missing owner or unfinished subcase refuses qualification.",
    "The aggregate binds the checked-out source and workflow head, exact named source-file hashes, published producer pin and checksums, platform and mode. Missing, cancelled or failed groups cannot produce a successful aggregate.",
    "The original four Durable Work Recovery application owners retain their original five-minute process command. Their selector is explicit and their results now refuse missing tests or skips.",
    "Existing five-platform native jobs, Windows shards, required names and backend owner jobs remain present. Build now requires Complete Application Recovery.",
    "The application group uses the existing 30-minute whole-Go allowance. Full embedded activation retains its original 420-second operation deadline; all in-test deadlines remain unchanged. The 50-minute job bound includes cold builds, native tests and artifact upload."
  ],
